[b]Download status:[/b] The 0.1.2-dev.36 file is held by Nexus automated safety checks and is waiting for manual review; it cannot be downloaded until the review is finished. Nexus holds packages for reasons such as included executables. VirusTotal results for every runtime file of 0.1.2-dev.36 (20 October 2026): version.dll 0/71, EpochPact.Core.dll 0/71, EpochPact.exe 0/71, EpochPact.MelonBridge.dll 0/71. These results do not prove a file is safe; they are listed so you can check them. [url=https://github.com/falorfrozen-cmd/EpochPact/releases]GitHub releases[/url].

[size=6][b]EpochPact — Your timeline. Your rules.[/b][/size]
An external desktop toolkit for Last Epoch offline players, with Chronoforge and Void Atlas themes. Adjust your session, customize character bonuses and manage progression from one interface in English, Turkish or Russian.

[b]Release: 0.1.2-dev.36 | Author: Falor | Windows x64 | Offline only[/b]
Supported installation: Steam Last Epoch [b]1.5.2.1, build 25816319[/b] (internal version 1.5.2.2). Other builds are not certified. The app verifies GameAssembly.dll before installation or modded launch. This is a public development release with a known full-game-exit crash described below.

[b]New in 0.1.2-dev.36:[/b] the game folder needs only one file, [b]version.dll[/b]. The mod's core is now built into it, so there is no separate EpochPact.Core.dll beside it. Updating with the app removes the core file left by earlier releases and keeps a backup.

[size=5][b]Features included[/b][/size]
[list]
[*][b]Progression and combat:[/b] enemy/mote XP and collected gold up to 100x; movement-speed and cooldown tuning. General session sliders apply automatically after an edit. Quest XP is not included in the enemy/mote multiplier.[/*]
[*][b]Loot and pickup:[/b] item quantity up to 25x, rarity up to 10x, automatic pickup, loot-filter support, Unique LP thresholds and selected T7 affixes.[/*]
[*][b]Character bonuses:[/b] 206 character-sheet mappings with search, flat bonuses or percentage increases, live reads and reset. Some game stats share one native key; the interface identifies this. More-mode settings are available only where supported.[/*]
[*][b]Crafting workshop:[/b] Forging Potential costs, Glyph of Hope/Despair probabilities, shard/rune/glyph preservation and crafting level controls. Uses the selected item in the game's Forge; it does not invent items or grant materials on startup.[/*]
[*][b]Campaign and waypoints:[/b] complete eligible main/side quests with their normal rewards, raise the character to at least level 55 and unlock 109 waypoint scenes. Completed quests do not pay out again.[/*]
[*][b]Monolith control:[/b] Normal/Empowered unlocks, timeline selection, Corruption, Stability and Stability gain multipliers. Opening a timeline or focusing an existing Echo travels to Traveler's Rest first; refreshing data does not travel or start an Echo.[/*]
[*][b]World and exploration:[/b] monster density up to 5x, including Monolith packs, zone-map reveal and browsing/focusing existing Echo rewards. The Navigator does not generate arbitrary new Echoes.[/*]
[*][b]Circle of Fortune:[/b] rank, Favor, Reputation, prophecies, lenses and gain/reward/quality multipliers.[/*]
[*][b]Unique Atlas and Stash Assistant:[/b] Unique/Set catalog, owned/missing/wishlist views, duplicate comparisons and actual affix/LP inspection. Protection reminders are informational; they do not lock items in-game.[/*]
[*][b]Inventory, loot and combat windows:[/b] Sell all and automatic inventory sorting; loot filter colours, rules in item tooltips and stash tabs; compact loot feed and damage meter windows with damage by type; death recap; interface fonts; Weaver's Will controls; Season 5 settings.[/*]
[*][b]Player setup and recovery:[/b] select any supported Steam library/custom game path, install the included runtime, launch offline, save setting profiles and use progression recovery backups.[/*]
[/list]Weaver and Merchant's Guild management are [b]not implemented[/b]; informational faction details are not advertised as working management tools.

[size=5][b]Requirements[/b][/size]
[list]
[*]A legitimate Steam installation of the exact supported Last Epoch build above.[/*]
[*]Windows 10/11 x64, Microsoft Edge WebView2 Runtime and .NET Framework 4.8.[/*]
[*]The included runtime file [b]version.dll[/b] (EpochPact's loader, with the mod's core built into it).[/*]
[/list]Python is bundled; no separate Python install is needed. No MelonLoader, BepInEx, development SDK or additional mod loader is required; if MelonLoader 0.7.3 is already installed, Install mod keeps it and adds EpochPact's own bridge instead. [url=https://developer.microsoft.com/microsoft-edge/webview2/]Official WebView2 download[/url]. Online play is unsupported and native changes are gated to offline characters. Do not combine loaders that require the same version.dll.

[size=5][b]Install[/b][/size]
Download the Main file and extract the whole ZIP to a normal writable folder, not into the game folder. Keep the [b]EpochPact[/b] app folder complete, including EpochPact.exe.config and _internal.
1. Close Last Epoch. Run [b]EpochPact/EpochPact.exe[/b].
2. Open Game setup, press Browse, select your installed Last Epoch.exe, then Save path. Any Steam library or custom folder is supported.
3. Press [b]Install mod[/b]. It copies one file, version.dll, into the game folder. If Windows denies the installation, use the explicit Install as administrator action and approve Windows yourself. Do not run the entire interface as administrator by default.
4. Press Launch offline and load an offline character.

[b]Manual alternative:[/b] copy [b]Manual Installation/version.dll[/b] into the folder containing Last Epoch.exe (Steam > Manage > Browse local files). That one file is the whole mod. Check your game version against supported-game-builds.json first; a manual copy cannot check the game build. Never overwrite another mod's loader. The app detects an exactly copied version.dll as installed.

[b]Use Manual Download.[/b] This package is not configured for a mod manager. The ZIP contains README.md with full instructions, third-party notices, a runtime manifest and SHA256SUMS.txt. No game executables, GameAssembly.dll, game metadata, saves, development SDKs, tests or private logs are distributed.

[size=5][b]Update, rollback and uninstall[/b][/size]
To update, close Last Epoch, extract the new ZIP and press Reinstall / update mod in its app. Updating from an earlier release removes the EpochPact/EpochPact.Core.dll it left in the game folder; the previous mod files are kept under EpochPact/install-backups. Apps from 0.1.2-dev.22 on can also update themselves from GitHub (New version > Install update). To update by hand, replace version.dll and delete a leftover EpochPact/EpochPact.Core.dll. Never mix app and loader versions.

To roll back, install an earlier release with its own app (it replaces this version.dll), or restore the files from an install-backups folder by following its README with the matching older app.

To uninstall, close both programs and press Game setup > Uninstall mod. It removes only EpochPact's version.dll (or its MelonLoader bridge) and an EpochPact.Core.dll left by an earlier release. By hand, remove only those EpochPact files, plus your extracted app folder if desired. Keep save-recovery backups. Do not delete another loader or the entire shared mod directory. Uninstall does not remove player saves; mod logs/backups/preferences may remain.

[size=5][b]Controls and persistence[/b][/size]
No required in-game hotkey: use the external sidebar. General session settings apply automatically; character bonuses use Apply/Reset. Permanent rewards, quest completion, balances and unlocks require their explicit action buttons. Opening the app never completes quests or grants rewards.

Keep the game unpaused and let loading finish. If background execution is unavailable, return to the game; do not repeatedly click a timed-out save action. Closing EpochPact resets controls changed in that session to neutral defaults and removes its own actor bonuses, without closing the game. It does not restore a different tool's earlier non-default values. Permanent progression/rewards remain. Cleanup failure keeps the app open with an error. Profiles do not automatically replay save actions.

[size=5][b]Verification and known issues — please read[/b][/size]
[list]
[*]0.1.2-dev.36 release checks: 346 Python tests, 235 JavaScript tests, 22 native test programs, 24 compiled-package checks and 4 frozen-app connection checks passed; Windows Defender found no threats in the ZIP. The one-file loader was tested in Last Epoch 1.5.2.1 on an isolated test character (connect, read, write and a clean game exit), and an earlier release can still replace or remove it.[/*]
[*]Earlier 1.5.2.1 smoke test: the packaged EXE applied Intelligence +100%, confirmed [b]11 → 22[/b] in the native game getter, and successfully read Monolith, CoF, crafting, map and loot state. Normal EXE close reset Intelligence to 11 and XP from 2x to 1x while the game remained running.[/*]
[*]The retained full-feature gameplay audit was on [b]1.5.2[/b]: 134 stat types/247 exact keys, 4,449 stat checks, Monolith selection flows and an actual completed Echo. It is not a full re-certification of every feature on 1.5.2.1.[/*]
[*]Installer fixtures cover custom/Unicode paths, unsupported builds, foreign loaders, partial-failure recovery, update-backup restoration and updating from the two-file layout of earlier releases; real UAC interaction is not certified.[/*]
[*]Actual game-folder manual copy/update/uninstall preserved the game EXE, GameAssembly.dll and all 54 original save files. Temporary test saves were archived and original bytes restored. These file-operation checks are separate from game loading.[/*]
[*][b]Full game exit can still fail with 0xC0000005.[/b] On 1.5.2.1 one measured exit returned zero and a second returned 0xC0000005. Earlier tests also failed with EpochPact removed. The cause is not established; this is not a zero-crash release. Desktop-app close and full-game exit are separate outcomes.[/*]
[*]Not every combat consumer, crafting path, mod combination or PC configuration has been verified. Unsupported game updates are refused by the app. Manual users must check compatibility before installing.[/*]
[*]Unsigned EXE/DLL files may require a security review. Do not disable antivirus or assume a warning is a false positive. Report the exact file/hash and warning.[/*]
[/list][url=https://github.com/falorfrozen-cmd/EpochPact/blob/main/docs/nexus/verification.md]Detailed release verification[/url].

[size=5][b]Credits, AI disclosure and permissions[/b][/size]
Created by Falor. Community-made; not affiliated with Eleventh Hour Games. AI-assisted code/UI and AI-generated background/promotional artwork are disclosed. Images labelled “actual interface” are captures of the running player app; promotional artwork is labelled separately and is not a gameplay screenshot.

The [url=https://github.com/falorfrozen-cmd/EpochPact/tree/d497721574e59a56a515a2fe48b81406438fbc83]0.1.2-dev.36 source[/url] contains the native core, loader, UI/backends and build scripts. It does not include the game's proprietary binaries/metadata or private test saves. Public source access does not automatically grant reupload/asset redistribution rights. See DISTRIBUTION-PERMISSIONS.txt, THIRD-PARTY-NOTICES.txt and INTER-OFL.txt for permissions and bundled runtime/font credits.

[size=5][b]Support[/b][/size]
[url=https://discord.gg/q6aexZZSAf]Discord support[/url] | [url=https://github.com/falorfrozen-cmd/EpochPact]GitHub source and releases[/url]
Report EpochPact version, game version/Steam build, Windows version, installation method, exact action/error text, and whether the problem happened during gameplay, app close or full game exit. Include a screenshot if useful. Remove names/private paths from log extracts; do not post entire saves or private logs publicly.
